// RFC 0016 K4 "Families match ports": VertexLitGeneric in the combos the
// core's `vertexlit` family claims (base texture, $color and $alpha, alpha
// test, translucency, half-Lambert) under Source's vertex lighting: the
// ambient cube and up to four point, spot and directional lights. The legacy
// port draws them (run with --extra-arg=-vklegacyvertexlit; its pixels are
// judged against the retail D3D9 bytecode) and records the port pixels the
// family suite compares with (tools/render/family_port_pixels.py). Quads are
// in clip space (identity transforms), so the lights are in clip space too.
// VertexLitGeneric ignores $vertexcolor and $vertexalpha's vertex data
// (vertexlitgeneric_dx9_helper.cpp), though $vertexalpha still selects
// blending; vertexlit_vertexcolor_ignored pins that. Bump maps, env maps,
// detail, self-illumination and $phong are not claimed; their cases stay in
// ../vertexlitgeneric.vdf and ../forced/.
"LegacyShaderCases"
{
